-- title:
--   The j-function as an unramified uniformiser lift at a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a positive integer $N$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ that is algebraically closed, a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ together with the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \bmod q = (X_1^q - X_2)(X_1 - X_2^q)$ for it, and the integrality hypotheses `hα`, `hβ` saying that the Hecke maps $\overline{\alpha}$, $\overline{\beta}$ at level $N$ and prime $q$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ have integral underlying ring homomorphisms; let $P$ be a place specialisation for these data, so in particular $P$ carries a map $\mathrm{sp}$ from places of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-function field $\overline{\mathcal F}_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` to places of $\mathcal F_N(k) = k(j(\mathsf q), j(\mathsf q^N))$ and the pole-comparison axioms `d0_j_pole` etc. Let $w$ be a place of $\mathcal F_N(k)$ over $k$ lying in `ssPlaces q N k`, i.e. satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace q N k`, and assume that $\bar j - \bar j^{\,q^2}$ has order exactly $1$ at $w$ and at $\varphi \cdot w$, where $\varphi$ is the semilinear automorphism `arithFrobC q k N` of $\mathcal F_N(k)$ acting on Laurent coefficients by the Frobenius of $k$ and $\bar j$ is the Laurent series `jqModC k`. The conclusion asserts the existence of $g_0 \in \mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$, $y \in A((\mathsf q))$, $g \in \overline{\mathcal F}_N$ and $\bar g \in \mathcal F_N(k)$ such that $g_0$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldFull N` (the subfield of $\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ generated by the divisor expansions at level $N$), $g$ equals the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of $g_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$, the coefficientwise image of $y$ under the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is that same series, $\bar g$ is the coefficientwise reduction `coeffMap red` of $y$, both $w$ and $\varphi \cdot w$ give order $1$ to $\bar g - \bar g^{\,q^2}$, and $g$ lies in the valuation subring of every place $U$ of $\overline{\mathcal F}_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ for which $P.\mathrm{sp}\,U = w$, or the geometric-level Frobenius `frobOnPlacesGeomLevel` of $P.\mathrm{sp}\,U$ equals $w$, or $P.\mathrm{sp}\,U$ equals the geometric-level Frobenius of $w$.
--
--   This is the unramified case of the construction of a uniformiser at a supersingular point that lifts to characteristic zero with integral $\mathsf q$-expansion: when $\bar j - \bar j^{\,q^2}$ already has a simple zero at $w$ and at its Frobenius translate, the $\mathsf q$-expansion of $j$ itself serves as the lift. It feeds the construction of prolongation tuples with non-empty inertia-fixed node coordinates at level one, used in the comparison of the geometric and arithmetic Frobenius actions on supersingular points.
